.TH PICK3D 1
.SH NAME
pick3d \- everything hangs off a point
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/pick3d
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pick3D
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Pick3D.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
"A whimsical program which demonstrates some techniques."  Fifty points,
twenty circles, twenty lines and ten sprites \- and nothing holds a
coordinate except a point.  A circle is a pointer to a point and a
radius; a line is two pointers; a sprite is a pointer, a picture and a
matrix.  Drag one point and everything hanging off it moves, with no
update pass and no dependency list, because the drawing reads through the
pointer.
.PP
The sprites turn because each keeps its own matrix and multiplies it by
its own increment once a frame.  The original is candid that this is not
a good idea \- the step is whatever the refresh rate happened to be, and
rounding error accumulates in the matrix \- and it is reproduced as
written.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Drag the nearest point
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/pick3d.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR wm (1)
